program            = 002_typeof
area               = 08_gcc_extensions
description        = GCC typeof and __typeof__ applied to expressions and declarations, folded and volatile-runtime variants
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_audit_flags     = -Wall -Wextra -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror
ub_notes           <<END
UB-GATE DEVIATION AND ITS REASON. Every program in area 08_gcc_extensions drops
-pedantic from the default warning gate. Reason: the constructs under test are
non-standard GCC extensions by definition, and -pedantic exists precisely to reject
them; retaining it would fail every program in the area for doing exactly what it is
meant to do. This is the only area-wide deviation in the corpus. No other warning is
relaxed: -Wall, -Wextra, -Wconversion, -Wsign-conversion, -Wshadow and -Werror are all
retained, and this program is clean under them at -O0, -O1 and -O2. Measured with
gcc 13.3.0.

UB-FREEDOM ARGUMENT. All arithmetic is on small int and unsigned int values far from
INT_MIN, INT_MAX and UINT_MAX, so there is no signed overflow; the unsigned multiplies
are modular by definition and do not wrap here in any case. No shift operator is used.
The only pointers are fp and fq, both of which point at the live local fa; they are
dereferenced only while fa is in scope, no one-past-end pointer is formed, and no
pointer value is ever printed. There is no aliasing violation, since fa is accessed
only as int. Every object is initialized before it is read, including the swap
temporary. No object is modified twice between sequence points: TO_SWAP performs its
three assignments as separate full statements inside a do/while(0). Every printf call
receives at most one side-effecting argument. Nothing depends on padding bytes or on the
addresses of unrelated objects. Macro locals sw_t and ad_t are uniquely prefixed and
neither macro is nested inside itself, so -Wshadow is not tripped.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Nothing implementation-defined is observed, so no target restriction is needed and all
four targets are compared. The four rank checks are deliberately expressed as
SELF-REFERENTIAL RELATIONS rather than absolute widths: each compares sizeof of the type
typeof produced against sizeof of the type it should have produced, so each is trivially
1 on every target. This matters because sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) were measured as
4 on i686 and 8 on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64; printing sizeof(long) directly would give
8 on three targets and 4 on i686, and asserting sizeof(long) > sizeof(int) would be true
on three targets and false on i686. Either would make oracle (b) report a divergence
caused by the test rather than the compiler. The relational form is target-independent,
including on i686 where long and int are the same width. Plain char is never used, so the
measured char-signedness difference is not reached: char is signed on x86_64 and i686 but
unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64. Only the pointed-to value is printed, never a pointer.
Output is identical on all four targets at all three optimization levels.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
to_folded_b=2
to_folded_c=42
to_folded_d=100
to_folded_unsigned=15
to_folded_deref=40
to_folded_elem=41
to_folded_add=42
to_folded_swap=22 11
to_same_as_int=1
to_same_as_ptr=1
to_long_rank=1
to_unsigned_rank=1
to_runtime_c=42
to_runtime_d=80
to_runtime_unsigned=15
to_runtime_add=42
to_runtime_swap=22 11
END
